g\", \"developer-tools\", \"2026\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Stealing Reasoning Traces from Proprietary LLM APIs\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Researchers found they could extract encrypted chain-of-thought blocks from Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google by replaying traces into weaker models and jailbreaking them. The vulnerability has since been fixed.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/#Aug. 11, 2026\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"security\", \"jailbreaking\", \"reasoning-traces\", \"llm-security\", \"paper-review\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"There are no lossless transformations of natural-language text\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"Sophie Alpert's internal policy on acceptable use of AI writing by engineers. Every rewrite changes meaning, and information is lost when AI rewrites text without detailed understanding of what you're trying to communicate.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"Sophie Alpert (via Simon Willison)\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/#Aug. 11, 2026\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"writing\", \"ai-misuse\", \"llms\", \"documentation\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"I Tested 12 AI Dev Tools. I Kept Three.\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"A Medium article reviewing 12 AI coding tools including Claude Code, Cursor, Ollama, Copilot, Windsurf, and Cline. Only three earned a permanent place in the author's workflow.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"Medium Author (via Hacker News)\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://medium.com/@kuldeepjadeja7/i-tested-12-ai-dev-tools-i-kept-three-874476cef1c7\",\n    58→    \"pub